{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"fiifi-goes-back-for-his-book","version":1,"title":"Fiifi Goes Back for His Book","ageTiers":["5-6","7-8"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"Fiifi was in a hurry. His friends were already at the school gate, and the bell was about to ring.","sentences":["Fiifi was in a hurry.","His friends were already at the school gate, and the bell was about to ring."],"image":"sha256:f42cb3ceada297219f268d671658035d638024ef6cf562dac43f060e5130c066","alt":"A boy with a backpack runs along a village road towards a school gate.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:2def74702b1f9fad1d1205b53ac0620886b81c9f7e6cce397b472ea3c987955f","durationMs":7120,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2015],[2015,7120]],"words":[[0,360],[360,576],[576,720],[720,864],[864,2015],[2015,2231],[2231,2734],[2734,3022],[3022,3525],[3525,3669],[3669,3885],[3885,4317],[4317,4964],[4964,5180],[5180,5396],[5396,5684],[5684,5900],[5900,6260],[6260,6404],[6404,7120]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"He ran past the mango tree and the kenkey seller. Then he stopped. His heart went thump. His reading book was still on the kitchen table!","sentences":["He ran past the mango tree and the kenkey seller.","Then he stopped.","His heart went thump.","His reading book was still on the kitchen table!"],"image":"sha256:e591b03282b1253e2ce74bb0f35856844323c273751f27b3f362bf3050316b8a","alt":"The boy stops suddenly in the road with a shocked face as a woman with a basket looks on.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:d4b7bb2dd4409e2cfa17b0ef4af4975999e3617ec2cc9a51b20a3b70a5a0d55b","durationMs":11240,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3822],[3822,5657],[5657,7797],[7797,11240]],"words":[[0,153],[153,382],[382,688],[688,917],[917,1299],[1299,1605],[1605,1834],[1834,2063],[2063,2522],[2522,3822],[3822,4128],[4128,4281],[4281,5657],[5657,5886],[5886,6268],[6268,6574],[6574,7797],[7797,8026],[8026,8561],[8561,8867],[8867,9096],[9096,9478],[9478,9631],[9631,9860],[9860,10395],[10395,11240]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"‘If I go back, I will be late,’ thought Fiifi. ‘If I do not go back, I will have no book.’ What should he do?","sentences":["‘If I go back, I will be late,’ thought Fiifi.","‘If I do not go back, I will have no book.’ What should he do?"],"image":"sha256:7adc667da77b848a6f39aa3cffd69cbf576cf1e3e12c36d15b67b792d4e0c6e4","alt":"The boy stands in the middle of the road looking in both directions.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:cb33d026188267a2f34bf01b27d2ee8ac90dcd3b688a8a7f10402db3e00e6b49","durationMs":9600,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4326],[4326,9600]],"words":[[0,157],[157,314],[314,471],[471,1179],[1179,1336],[1336,1651],[1651,1808],[1808,2516],[2516,3067],[3067,4326],[4326,4483],[4483,4640],[4640,4797],[4797,5033],[5033,5190],[5190,5898],[5898,6055],[6055,6370],[6370,6685],[6685,6842],[6842,8022],[8022,8337],[8337,8809],[8809,8966],[8966,9600]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"He remembered Grandmother’s favourite saying. ‘Se wo were fi na wosankofa a yenkyi.’ It means: ‘It is not wrong to go back for what you forgot.’","sentences":["He remembered Grandmother’s favourite saying.","‘Se wo were fi na wosankofa a yenkyi.’ It means: ‘It is not wrong to go back for what you forgot.’"],"image":"sha256:b08cf4d77c62aa40260344b95f25366701636883815e701bccb1053d5d02e2e3","alt":"A memory bubble shows the grandmother smiling over the boy’s head.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:291fee45d764e21677eb9470957d0975ef312f89f17be8b70c39457001ed3c1c","durationMs":12960,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4500],[4500,12960]],"words":[[0,180],[180,1080],[1080,2160],[2160,2970],[2970,4500],[4500,4680],[4680,4860],[4860,5220],[5220,5400],[5400,5580],[5580,6390],[6390,6570],[6570,8100],[8100,8280],[8280,9180],[9180,9360],[9360,9540],[9540,9810],[9810,10260],[10260,10440],[10440,10620],[10620,10980],[10980,11250],[11250,11610],[11610,11880],[11880,12960]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"Fiifi ran home as fast as his legs could go. The book was on the table, right where he had left it. He grabbed it and ran back.","sentences":["Fiifi ran home as fast as his legs could go.","The book was on the table, right where he had left it.","He grabbed it and ran back."],"image":"sha256:8963943a054baeb9961d85282e67de4f193c2bd587d547bdf8d61ba792ba2362","alt":"The boy picks up a book from a kitchen table and rushes out of the door.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:854674c0a030d3b2c03bee4dd626b508f50606172eef12cce54f4e6b6f6fb8c2","durationMs":9800,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3420],[3420,7752],[7752,9800]],"words":[[0,380],[380,608],[608,912],[912,1064],[1064,1368],[1368,1520],[1520,1748],[1748,2052],[2052,2432],[2432,3420],[3420,3648],[3648,3952],[3952,4180],[4180,4332],[4332,4560],[4560,5320],[5320,5700],[5700,6080],[6080,6232],[6232,6460],[6460,6764],[6764,7752],[7752,7904],[7904,8436],[8436,8588],[8588,8816],[8816,9044],[9044,9800]]}}},{"n":6,"text":"At the gate, the bell rang. Fiifi arrived out of breath, but just in time. Mr Darko smiled and said, ‘Good morning, Fiifi.’","sentences":["At the gate, the bell rang.","Fiifi arrived out of breath, but just in time.","Mr Darko smiled and said, ‘Good morning, Fiifi.’"],"image":"sha256:983499ca05668652f87599586de67430d3e6691f8d0031fef0c5a92eda30a6a7","alt":"The boy reaches the school gate with the book while the teacher smiles.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:3d77166adf16539994efe70fd69bf1af638e2f192c6b0f30334db9e81ad38777","durationMs":11640,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2992],[2992,7315],[7315,11640]],"words":[[0,166],[166,415],[415,1163],[1163,1412],[1412,1745],[1745,2992],[2992,3408],[3408,3990],[3990,4239],[4239,4405],[4405,5320],[5320,5569],[5569,5902],[5902,6068],[6068,7315],[7315,7481],[7481,7897],[7897,8396],[8396,8645],[8645,9393],[9393,9726],[9726,10724],[10724,11640]]}}},{"n":7,"text":"That evening, Fiifi packed his bag the night before and put his reading book on top.","sentences":["That evening, Fiifi packed his bag the night before and put his reading book on top."],"image":"sha256:fffd737792d97b6d4011117dbf0703421a02b9348baaf3ea4ffa3fceff54df50","alt":"The boy places a book carefully on top of his school bag by the door.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:144cac9d0652962eed798d54b8dd728bc92b66d530d86edec6a8fed77f2f6982","durationMs":6480,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,6480]],"words":[[0,332],[332,1329],[1329,1744],[1744,2242],[2242,2491],[2491,2740],[2740,2989],[2989,3404],[3404,3902],[3902,4151],[4151,4400],[4400,4649],[4649,5231],[5231,5563],[5563,5729],[5729,6480]]}}},{"n":8,"text":"Grandmother laughed. ‘Going back was wise, but remembering the first time is even wiser!’ Fiifi grinned. ‘Sankofa and a packed bag!’ The end.","sentences":["Grandmother laughed.","‘Going back was wise, but remembering the first time is even wiser!’ Fiifi grinned.","‘Sankofa and a packed bag!’ The end."],"image":"sha256:39cdb196f7919623737f0ca995cb5229582a996b4bdde062ea2e5cbb2567fe31","alt":"The grandmother and boy laugh together beside a packed school bag.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:a3ee37ffcb4d7489944e618d8696170fda8f4e6b8692e9e49b60abee1fd32ecc","durationMs":15680,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2756],[2756,11497],[11497,15680]],"words":[[0,1045],[1045,2756],[2756,3231],[3231,3611],[3611,3896],[3896,4751],[4751,5036],[5036,6081],[6081,6366],[6366,6841],[6841,7221],[7221,7411],[7411,7791],[7791,9311],[9311,9786],[9786,11497],[11497,12162],[12162,12447],[12447,12637],[12637,13207],[13207,14537],[14537,14822],[14822,15680]]}}}],"activities":[{"id":"sankofa-c1","type":"comprehension","afterPage":2,"question":"What did Fiifi forget?","options":["His reading book","His lunch","His shoes"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"sankofa-p1","type":"prediction","af